  "result": "Intl.Segmenter now passes all of `intl402/Segmenter/` (158 runs, 0 failures), and `cargo clippy` and `cargo build` are clean. I ran `cargo fmt` last and did not re-run the tests or clippy after it.\n\nI addressed the reviewer's points from attempt 554:\n- **Locale:** Word and sentence segmenters are built from the resolved locale through ICU4X. ICU4X has no per-locale grapheme data, so grapheme segmentation is the same for every locale (noted in a comment). A data-load failure returns `not_implemented`.\n- **Caching:** Boundaries are computed once in `segment()` and shared with the iterator through an `Arc`, so `next()` and `containing()` no longer re-segment the string.\n- **`isWordLike`:** In ICU4X the word type belongs to the segment ending at the boundary, and `isWordLike` now uses that boundary list.\n- **Constructor and slots:** The `GetOption` default path is kept. The `unwrap_or_default` fallback is replaced by a `not_implemented` error when the slots are missing.\n\nI used `Arc` instead of `Rc` because the native-slot types must be `Send`.",
